<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Koca Sinan Pasha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1506–<a href="/years/1596">1596</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Koca Sinan Pasha was an Ottoman general and statesman of Albanian origin. He reconquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> from the Zaydi rebels in 1569 to 1571 and in 1574 took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-goulette">La Goulette</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hafsid-dynasty">Hafsid dynasty</a>. He later served five times as grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> and led campaigns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/long-turkish-war">Long Turkish War</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and Wallachia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/koca-sinan-pasha.jpg" alt="Koca Sinan Pasha" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arolsen_Klebeband_02_327.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
